Z||000001||ray b||03-10-2001||11:36 PM||||your are in land of snow so should be normal now to be cool but  do you have a stat in it now? some are removed by frist owner. check under cap on motor  with it cold. then pull out and put in pot in water on stove and heat to boil. it should open before it boils. replace and add water or anti-f. stat will help it run better and should be in it.<p>[This message has been edited by ray b (edited 03-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rhpetterson||03-11-2001||12:08 AM||||there is a stat in it but the gauge inside the car should move alittle during operation souldnt it/?? <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>your are in land of snow so should be normal now to be cool but  do you have a stat in it now? some are removed by frist owner. check under cap on motor  with it cold. then pull out and put in pot in water on stove and heat to boil. it should open before it boils. replace and add water or anti-f. stat will help it run better and should be in it.<P>[This message has been edited by ray b (edited 03-10-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||03-11-2001||01:48 AM||||I had the same issue with my Formula.  The temp guage would barely come off the 100 mark. I figured the previous owner put in a 160 therostat, or removed it altogether.  Well, it had the factory 195 in it.  I replaced it anyway, and not my temp comes right up to normal and stays there.  I may go with a lower one for summer, if needed, but the 195 is fine for now.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||03-11-2001||07:01 PM||||I also had problems with slow warm up...<BR>Replace the thermostat and be warm!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||ToddAsh||03-11-2001||08:45 PM||||Mine took about 15 minutes to get heat,put in new thermostat,now it's great. Todd||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ed||03-11-2001||10:25 PM||||I had a '88 Dodge Caravan with the 3.0 V-6 which had it's thermostat fail open.  I was coming down a long cold mountain grade and the check engine light came on.  I checked codes and they indicated low temp.  So they can fail open and leave you with a cold engine.  ||||reg||1
